# Mine — AI-Native Data Migration Platform
# Architecture: Next.js App Router + Supabase (auth, DB, storage) + Claude API
# Deployed on Vercel at trymine.ai

## Stack Rules
- Next.js App Router with Server Components by default, 'use client' only when needed
- Supabase for auth, database (PostgreSQL), and file storage
- Claude API (Sonnet) for AI features — all calls server-side only
- Tailwind CSS for styling
- TypeScript strict mode

## Supabase Client Rules (CRITICAL)
- THREE Supabase clients exist, never mix them:
  1. `lib/supabase/client.ts` — browser only, uses NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY, respects RLS
  2. `lib/supabase/server.ts` — Server Components/Actions only, uses anon key + user cookies, respects RLS
  3. `lib/supabase/admin.ts` — Server-side admin only, uses SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY, BYPASSES RLS
- NEVER import `lib/supabase/admin.ts` in any client component
- NEVER import `lib/supabase/client.ts` in any server component
- NEVER use SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY in client-side code

## Security Rules
- NEVER expose ANTHROPIC_API_KEY or SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY to the client
- Only NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL and NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY get the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix
- All Claude API calls go through lib/ai/claude.ts (server-side only)
- Always validate and sanitize CSV data before storing
- Always run validateGeneratedSQL() before executing any AI-generated SQL
- Never log API keys, user passwords, or full JWT tokens
- Use parameterized queries — never string-concatenate user input into SQL

## File Structure Convention
- app/ — Next.js App Router pages and layouts
- components/ — Reusable React components
- lib/ — Utilities, Supabase clients, AI helpers, types
- lib/supabase/ — Supabase client files (client.ts, server.ts, admin.ts)
- lib/ai/ — Claude API integration
- lib/types/ — TypeScript type definitions
- supabase/migrations/ — SQL migration files

## Database Pattern
- Every table has RLS enabled
- All data traces back to projects.user_id = auth.uid()
- Use UUID primary keys with gen_random_uuid()
- Timestamps use TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT now()
- Foreign keys use ON DELETE CASCADE

## Component Pattern
- Server Components by default (no directive needed)
- Add 'use client' only for interactive components (forms, dropdowns, click handlers)
- Use Server Actions for data mutations
- Use Supabase server client in Server Components and Server Actions
- Use Supabase browser client only in 'use client' components that need real-time or client-side queries
